[{'question': 'A guarded, standards-backed outer-pipe-diameter-to-DN retrieval alternate will improve candidate recall for valve tenders that specify an unambiguous pipe OD rather than DN, while preserving original-query reranking and selection.', 'findings': 'The GOST source lists 108 mm as a standard outside diameter; the pipe source identifies DN 108×3.5 as DN 100. The plan limits conversion to explicit OD context and this single documented mapping.', 'sources': [{'url': 'https://meganorm.ru/mega_doc/norm/gost_gosudarstvennyj-standart/0/gost_10704-91_mezhgosudarstvennyy_standart_truby_stalnye.html'}, {'url': 'https://tavago.ru/truby-i-fitingi/stalnye-truby/truby-stalnye-elektrosvarnye-gost-10704-91/truba-stal-elektrosvarnaya-pryamoshovnaya-dn-108kh3-5-du-100-gost-10704-91.html'}], 'origin': 'legacy-cycle-11'}, {'question': 'Does the 30с41нж designation define a flanged, wedge-gate, rising-stem DN/PN class that has a technically equivalent LD catalog family, rather than only a superficially similar gate valve?', 'findings': 'Reject the premise of an LD-family equivalence. 30с41нж is a steel wedge-gate family at PN 1.6 MPa (PN16), offered across DN sizes; manufacturer documentation identifies its flanged version and wedge construction. One manufacturer explicitly calls it flanged with a rising stem. However, the supplied LD catalog contains no gate-valve products: its only names containing «задвижк» are six LD Стриж ball valves described as «под задвижку», all with interflange connections. A ball valve, even at matching DN/PN, is not technically equivalent to a flanged rising-stem wedge gate valve. Also, DN is not encoded as one fixed value in 30с41нж; it must be supplied separately.', 'decision_impact': 'Do not add a designation-to-LD gate-valve alias or treat LD ball valves as substitutions for 30с41нж. Match only if a tender explicitly permits an alternative valve type; otherwise this is a catalog no-match for the LD corpus.', 'unresolved': 'The designation’s exact connection configuration should still be verified against the procurement specification: the MZTA family page lists both welded and flanged connections, while the conventional 30с41нж product documentation describes the flanged rising-stem variant. This does not affect the lack of an LD wedge-gate family.', 'sources': [{'url': 'https://mztpa.ru/catalog/products/1/5/15', 'claim': 'Official manufacturer page: 30с41нж is a steel wedge-gate family at PN 1.6 MPa; it gives DN 50–400 examples, identifies flanged dimensions, and lists flanged and welded connection options for the family.', 'quality': 'official', 'confidence': 0.96}, {'url': 'https://www.ptza.ru/30s41nzh-zadvizhka-klinovaya/', 'claim': 'Official manufacturer page: 30с41нж is described as a flanged wedge gate valve with a rising stem, PN 1.6 MPa, with a DN range rather than one fixed DN.', 'quality': 'official', 'confidence': 0.94}], 'origin': 'cycle-01'}, {'question': 'What recurring real-tender failure classes suggest the next bounded hypothesis?', 'findings': 'Derived the 130 review cases from the intact full corpus minus the 90 labels and 33 provisional cases because the provided review-pool gzip has CRC/length corruption. Main classes: (1) 71 ball-valve rows, heavily concentrated in threaded inch-size, endpoint, handle, and third-party model nomenclature (IVR/VALTEC); current canonicalization produces no meaningful retrieval alternate for these. The LD catalog contains 647 brass ball valves and itself expresses inch↔DN forms, so this is a genuine catalog-language mismatch. (2) 33 filter and many service/maintenance rows (installation, removal, repair, ТО) are requests for work, consumables, or water-treatment equipment rather than a sellable LD catalog item; retrieval should not be pushed toward an unrelated product. (3) 20 butterfly-valve rows mix generic viable requests with third-party model/designation requests; 356 LD butterfly products exist, so model text may obscure otherwise useful family/DN/PN evidence. Promising directions: additive canonicalization of unambiguous threaded endpoint spellings (ВР/НР, вн-вн) and standard inch sizes into catalog-native DN/connection vocabulary; a conservative query-intent route for explicit service/maintenance actions; and a separately bounded manufacturer/model enrichment or model-token de-emphasis experiment for third-party branded products.', 'decision_impact': 'Prefer a retrieval-only, fail-open threaded/inch canonicalization experiment: it addresses the largest repeated viable-product class, aligns with the only previously accepted mechanism, and leaves reranking/selection unchanged. Keep service-intent routing as a distinct safety hypothesis rather than combining it, since prior selection-adjacent changes regressed. Treat external model lookup as lower-volume and higher-latency unless a later sample shows generic normalization cannot recover branded rows.', 'unresolved': 'The review-pool gzip is corrupt locally, though the full corpus supports exact reconstruction by id count. Need evaluate whether catalog-native endpoint/inch expansion improves candidate recall without crowding out candidates; do not assume branded models are technically interchangeable. Service rows may be procurement line items that intentionally include a product, so any intent router must be explicit-action-only and conservative.', 'sources': [], 'origin': 'attempt-01-research-first', 'kind': 'research-first'}, {'question': 'What recurring real-tender classes and current-pipeline gaps should inform the next bounded hypothesis?', 'findings': 'The intact corpus reconstructs 130 review rows (253 total minus 90 labelled and 33 provisional NOT_FOUND). Main classes: 53 ball-valve rows, including 42 threaded and 35 third-party-brand/model rows; 20 butterfly-valve rows, several branded; 33 filter rows, many cartridges/water-treatment rather than LD грязевики; and 18 explicit installation/repair/maintenance rows. The catalog has substantial ball-valve (14,433), butterfly-valve (356), and filter (129) coverage, but no matching third-party brand/model tokens (IVR, VALTEC, Tecofi, Kvant, etc.), so opaque model/order text can dominate retrieval despite otherwise usable generic requirements. Current canonicalization produces alternates for only 40/130 review rows. It also has a general lexical integrity flaw: its quantity/clause terminator can interpret the substring «ШТ.» inside a technical designation as a quantity marker, truncating «КШТ.11.050.025.ф/ф» to «Кран БИВАЛ К». The original query remains in retrieval, but the added alternate is degraded. Promising directions: (1) a bounded, additive model/order-token de-emphasis alternate that retains explicit product family, size, endpoint, material, control, and pressure facts without asserting cross-brand equivalence; (2) a generic token-boundary/quantity-parser correction so technical designations cannot be clipped; (3) separately, a conservative intent route for unambiguous service-only work or non-catalog consumables; (4) only if simpler normalization fails, runtime manufacturer/model enrichment for repeated branded families.', 'decision_impact': 'Prefer testing retrieval-only supplier/model-noise de-emphasis, with the untouched original query retained and no inferred specifications or final-selection changes. It targets a repeated 35-row class and differs from the previously rejected endpoint/inch expansion. Treat the designation-truncation repair as a small correctness fix or separate experiment. Keep service/consumable abstention isolated: some work lines include an underlying product, and prior selection-adjacent changes were risky.', 'unresolved': 'The review-pool gzip remains CRC-corrupt, though its intended set is exactly reconstructable from the other supplied files. Branded model strings may encode material, porting, or connection details not stated elsewhere; a de-emphasis alternate must therefore be additive and preserve all explicit non-model tokens. Filter rows need a product-vs-consumable distinction before any NOT_FOUND routing.', 'sources': [], 'origin': 'attempt-02-research-first', 'kind': 'research-first'}, {'question': 'What recurring real-tender failure classes and bounded directions should inform the next hypothesis?', 'findings': 'The intact corpus reconstructs the 130 review rows (253 total minus 90 labelled minus 33 provisional NOT_FOUND); the supplied review-pool gzip remains CRC-corrupt. The largest viable-looking unresolved class is branded threaded ball valves: 53 ball-valve rows, 42 with third-party brands, including 30 IVR rows. Current canonicalization emits an alternate for only 40/130 review rows, and none for representative IVR/VALTEC rows. Official manufacturer data shows the opaque IVR 954/956 codes carry material retrieval facts: full-bore threaded ball valve and F/F versus M/F endpoints; VALTEC VT.214 likewise identifies a ball valve with an internal-thread endpoint. LD has hundreds of brass threaded ball-valve products, including explicit В-В/В-Н and handle variants, so this is a real vocabulary/underspecification gap—not evidence that foreign branded products are automatically interchangeable with LD.\n\nA separate correctness defect is confirmed: the clause terminator treats the embedded «ШТ.» in a technical designation as a quantity token, reducing «Кран БИВАЛ КШТ.11.050.025.ф/ф 50х25 КОФ» to «Кран БИВАЛ К». This should be repaired by token-boundary parsing, not a designation-specific rule. The pool also contains 33 filter/water-treatment rows and explicit work rows; many are consumables or service requests, but a few service lines embed a product, so broad abstention is unsafe.\n\nPromising directions: (1) a bounded, fail-open runtime manufacturer/model enrichment path for extractable brand+model queries, using a trusted manufacturer source and adding only explicitly documented generic facts to an alternate retrieval query; retain the original query and final selection semantics. (2) A small generic quantity/clause-boundary correction that preserves technical designations in retrieval alternates. (3) A later conservative product-intent/uncertainty route restricted to unambiguous service-only or consumable-only queries. Do not repeat deterministic inch/endpoint expansion or generic supplier-token suppression: both have already been rejected by hidden safety gates.', 'decision_impact': 'The strongest new product opportunity is source-backed, additive enrichment of repeated branded model nomenclature, because a model code can resolve endpoint and bore facts that the tender omits. It has external dependency, latency, caching, and source-trust costs, and must never assert LD equivalence or override reranking. If the Planner wants the lowest-risk bounded experiment instead, select the generic designation/quantity parser repair; it is a correctness fix with narrower expected corpus impact. Keep service abstention separate from either retrieval experiment.', 'unresolved': 'Whether external enrichment improves LD candidate recall enough to justify runtime dependency is unmeasured; manufacturer documents establish source-product properties, not a suitable LD substitute. The CRC-corrupt review-pool artifact should be repaired separately, although its intended membership is reconstructable from the other corpus files.', 'sources': [{'url': 'https://www.ivrvalvole.it/media/pdf/schede/IVR_954_956_957.pdf', 'claim': 'Official IVR technical sheet identifies IVR 954/956/957 as full-bore threaded ball valves and distinguishes F/F, M/F, and M/M endpoints; it also provides Russian terminology.', 'quality': 'official', 'confidence': 0.98}, {'url': 'https://valtec.ru/document/Catalog_VALTEC.pdf?69a765ad99bad=', 'claim': 'Official VALTEC catalogue identifies VT.214 as a ball valve with a steel handle and internal-to-internal threaded connection.', 'quality': 'official', 'confidence': 0.95}], 'origin': 'attempt-03-research-first', 'kind': 'research-first'}]

RESEARCH CONTRACT
You are not choosing the next implementation. Your job is to build the best current causal understanding of the problem before the Planner chooses an experiment.

Start with evidence synthesis, not idea generation.

1. Inspect the current implementation, the real-task working corpus, compact experiment evidence, hypothesis/mechanism ledger available to the Planner, and prior research.
2. Treat every scientifically evaluated experiment as evidence about the system: what causal intervention changed, what end-to-end behavior improved, what regressed, what stayed flat, and whether different implementations produced the same directional outcome.
3. Group experiments by causal mechanism, not by filenames, feature names, or superficial implementation differences. If two changes act through essentially the same causal path, treat them as the same mechanism family.
4. Look explicitly for cross-experiment patterns. Repeated similar outcome signatures are evidence about the current causal model even when individual hypotheses had different names.
5. Do not optimize an intermediate metric in isolation. If a mechanism repeatedly improves an intermediate capability while failing end-to-end utility, reconsider the causal bottleneck instead of automatically proposing another nearby variant.
6. Do not repeat a tested mechanism merely because another implementation is available. A refinement is worthwhile only when new evidence changes a causal premise, directly addresses an observed failure mechanism, or provides substantial new information.
7. When a local family appears saturated, broaden the search space. Upstream, downstream, adjacent, or architectural mechanisms are admissible; current pipeline boundaries are not sacred.
8. Prefer experiments with high expected information gain: ask which bounded experiment would most reduce uncertainty between competing explanations of observed behavior.
9. Use real-task data to discover problem classes and practical value. Public and hidden-validation aggregates are regression evidence, not sources of benchmark-specific implementation ideas.
10. Do not prescribe a favored architecture in advance. Query understanding, parsing, aliases, retrieval, reranking, catalog representation, model use, external data, runtime enrichment, confidence/decision logic, representation changes, or pipeline restructuring are admissible only when evidence supports them.
11. Runtime lookup of a manufacturer/model/designation on the public internet and enrichment of an underspecified user query is allowed as one possible family, but it is NOT a prescribed answer.
12. Use the internet only when it can materially improve the next decision. Open at most 3 external sources and prefer primary/official evidence.
13. Do not edit repository files. Do not inspect hidden examples. Do not invent benchmark-specific rules or one-off mappings.

OUTPUT CONTRACT
- `evidence_patterns`: compact cross-experiment patterns. Cite prior experiment/cycle identifiers when available; distinguish observation from interpretation and give confidence.
- `candidate_directions`: 2-4 materially meaningful directions when evidence supports them. For each, state a stable causal `mechanism_family`, its relation to history, the causal mechanism, competing explanation, falsifier, and expected information gain.
- `findings`: concise synthesis of the strongest observations from code + real tender corpus + experiment evidence.
- `decision_impact`: tell the Planner what uncertainty/trade-off deserves the next experiment, without selecting an implementation for it.
- If evidence does not support another nearby refinement, say so explicitly. Do not manufacture novelty for its own sake.

Return the required JSON only.

