end-to-end uplift. The supplied review-pool gzip remains corrupt; membership is reconstructable from the intact all-rows, labels, and provisional-NOT_FOUND files. It is also unmeasured whether correcting the canonical alternate changes the final top-20, because the original query is retained and may already supply the needed candidate.","sources":[],"evidence_patterns":[{"pattern":"Narrow additive retrieval normalization has conditional value; semantic expansion is not generally beneficial.","supporting_experiments":["legacy-cycle-3 ACCEPTED: deterministic query canonicalization improved safely.","legacy-cycle-4 ACCEPTED: standalone WW expansion improved safely.","legacy-cycle-6 REJECTED: flanged-shorthand canonicalization regressed hidden safety.","legacy-cycle-9 REJECTED: standard-bore wording expansion was neutral.","legacy-cycle-17 REJECTED: installed-electric versus actuator-ready alternate had an unreliable catalog semantic premise."],"interpretation":"The successful causal path is preservation/translation of unambiguous catalog vocabulary, not adding plausible domain semantics. The present parser truncation directly destroys source evidence inside that proven retrieval-only path, so repairing it is materially different from adding another alias.","confidence":0.94},{"pattern":"Changes that alter candidate composition or final compatibility selection have repeatedly failed to improve end-to-end utility.","supporting_experiments":["legacy cycles 1-2: broad filtering and compatibility-evidence intervention regressed.","legacy-cycle-5 REJECTED: evidence-first reranker rubric regressed blind safety.","legacy-cycle-8 REJECTED: deterministic post-rerank compatibility substitution was neutral.","legacy-cycle-16 REJECTED: candidate diversification regressed public coverage.","legacy-cycle-7 REJECTED: catalog structural representation reduced hidden coverage."],"interpretation":"The evidence does not show that more candidate filtering, compatibility gating, prompt changes, diversification, or catalog rewriting is the current bottleneck. A new decision/abstention layer would need a sharply separable request-intent signal, not generic technical compatibility rules.","confidence":0.91},{"pattern":"Branded tender nomenclature is common, but prior genericization and external-fact enrichment were unsafe.","supporting_experiments":["attempt-01 alias_mapping REJECTED: threaded/inch expansion increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND rate by 0.04.","attempt-02 alias_mapping REJECTED: supplier/model-noise suppression increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND rate by 0.04.","attempt-03 alias_mapping REJECTED: trusted manufacturer/model facts increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND rate by 0.08."],"interpretation":"Opaque brand/model text is a real corpus mismatch, but making it more generic or importing source facts did not establish LD interchangeability and degraded safety. This points to underspecification/equivalence uncertainty rather than a simple lexical-recall deficit.","confidence":0.96},{"pattern":"A distinct non-catalog/service class is large enough to compete with more retrieval work.","supporting_experiments":["Real-corpus inspection: 33 review rows are filter/water-treatment related; examples include cartridges, filter media, water-treatment units, and service work.","Catalog inspection: zero catalog texts contain cartridge/ЭФГ or water-treatment terms; 129 filter entries are largely грязевики.","Real-corpus inspection: 11 review rows explicitly request removal, repair, installation, or maintenance."],"interpretation":"For many rows, better retrieval cannot create a compatible sellable LD product. Yet action words alone are insufficient, because some installation/removal lines mention a product family; any intervention must establish service-only or absent-capability evidence affirmatively.","confidence":0.88}],"candidate_directions":[{"mechanism_family":"query_evidence_preservation","history_relation":"REFINEMENT","causal_mechanism":"Repair structural line-item/quantity boundary parsing so a canonical retrieval alternate cannot stop inside an alphanumeric technical designation; retain the raw query, all existing canonical transformations, and final reranking behavior.","competing_explanation":"Because raw-query retrieval remains active, the damaged alternate may not materially affect candidate availability or final selection; the observed defect may be operationally harmless on most rows.","falsifier":"A stratified real-tender retrieval comparison shows that preserving affected designations does not add or improve viable family-consistent candidates in the pre-rerank pool, while public/hidden gates remain flat.","information_gain":"High confidence in correctness and moderate information gain: it isolates whether an established successful mechanism is currently losing evidence through parsing rather than through retrieval or reranking."},{"mechanism_family":"query_variant_evidence_fusion","history_relation":"NEW_LAYER","causal_mechanism":"Represent original and canonical retrieval hits as separate evidence channels through fusion, rather than collapsing each modality to one locally best rank before RRF; reward candidates corroborated by both query forms without removing candidates or changing reranker semantics.","competing_explanation":"The primary limitation may be candidate absence or reranker choice, so preserving alternate-query corroboration may not alter the fixed top-20 meaningfully; candidate-composition changes have previously been risky.","falsifier":"On a real-tender stratification of rows with canonical alternates, variant-aware fusion does not improve family/constraint-consistent candidate presence or rank, or it breaches public/hidden coverage or safety gates.","information_gain":"Moderate-to-high: it tests an untried architectural implication of the accepted canonicalization mechanism while avoiding another semantic expansion or index rebuild."},{"mechanism_family":"catalog_scope_and_request_intent","history_relation":"NEW_LAYER","causal_mechanism":"Use affirmative evidence of service-only procurement or a request category absent from the LD product taxonomy to route toward an uncertain/NOT_FOUND outcome, while allowing lines that name an actual purchasable product to continue through ordinary retrieval.","competing_explanation":"Tender work descriptions can embed an intended product, and catalog lexical fields can be noisy; a router could convert recoverable matches into wrong NOT_FOUND, reproducing prior selection-adjacent regressions.","falsifier":"A manually reviewed non-benchmark sample shows material overlap between the proposed service/absent-category cues and viable LD product requests, or regression gates show increased wrong-NOT_FOUND.","information_gain":"High: it separates genuine catalog noncoverage from retrieval failure in the sizeable consumable, water-treatment, and service portion of the real corpus."}]}
